---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const coreCompetencies = [
  "Spatial Computer Vision",
  "CV Model Fine-Tuning",
  "Human-in-the-loop (HITL) Evaluation",
  "Responsible AI & Privacy (PII Detection)",
  "3D Reconstruction & 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS)",
  "Generative AI (GenAI)",
  "Platform & Product Strategy",
  "API Design",
  "Pricing & Monetization (TSM/WTP)",
  "Cross Functional & Executive Leadership",
];

const companies = [
  {
    name: "Zillow Group",
    location: "Seattle, WA, USA",
    dates: "Mar 2019 - Present",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Principal Product Manager, Rich Media AI",
        dates: "Jan 2022 - Present",
        summary:
          "<strong>Product Lead for Zillow's Immersive Media Capture & Management Ecosystem across iOS, Android, Web, and Cloud APIs.</strong> Direct product strategy for Zillow 3D Home and SkyTour, leveraging Spatial Computer Vision, Generative AI, and 3D reconstruction pipelines to <strong>scale media throughput 20x (from 3K to 60K+ tours/month)</strong>. Eliminate physical capture friction and hardware barriers to drive creator adoption, while deploying responsible AI privacy safeguards for high-volume media partners that unblocked a strategic enterprise deal <strong>(50K+ annual tours, ~15% of platform volume)</strong>, while separately building self-serve support tooling that cut engineering support requests by <strong>87.7%</strong>.",
        bullets: [
          "<strong>Spatial CV & User Adoption Friction Removal:</strong> Replaced physical floor plan markers (mousepad/setup shots) by championing a spatial computer vision (CV) heuristic based on architectural invariants (door, kitchen cabinet and countertop heights); deployed after 6 months of rigorous validation testing, this method saved <strong>$268K/yr</strong> ($100k operational cost + $168k manual annotation cost), cut floor plan processing queue times by <strong>50% (7.0h → 3.7h)</strong>, and eliminated setup-related tour rejections by <strong>100%.</strong>",
          "<strong>Enterprise PII Blurring:</strong> Spearheaded automated AI privacy blurring (faces, license plates, diplomas) across 360° panoramas by fine-tuning an open-source CV model on 1,000+ panoramas; enforced a <strong>>90% precision gate</strong>, 2-month shadow pipeline deployment, and manual AI override UX in the dashboard, unblocking a strategic enterprise syndication deal that safeguarded <strong>50k+ tours annually (~15% of platform volume).</strong>",
          "<strong>Capture Guidance Redesign:</strong> Diagnosed ambiguous multi-panorama capture instructions as root cause of floor plan generation failures; redesigned in-app + video guidance around a connective shot heuristic (line-of-sight capture at doorways, standardized 12ft spacing) validated with applied science. Cut panoramas required per home <strong>~50% (50–60 → 25–30)</strong> and reduced floor plan generation failures from <strong>30% to under 5%</strong>, improving both photographer efficiency and product sentiment.",
          "<strong>Image Quality & GenAI Pipeline:</strong> Led a multi-year image quality transformation, combining home-grown Auto White Balance (AWB) and HDR merge algorithms with cloud GenAI enhancement pipelines; fine-tuned candidate generative models strictly on Zillow-licensed media to enforce data ethics, and architected a <strong>1-year Human-in-the-Loop (HITL) hallucination benchmarking framework</strong> with parallel shadow deployments to evaluate and de-risk model reliability prior to full rollout.",
          "<strong>SkyTour Rollout:</strong> Orchestrated the <strong>nationwide rollout of \"SkyTour\"</strong> (exterior virtual tour product based on 3D Gaussian Splatting / 3DGS technology), while maintaining a <strong>99% video upload success rate</strong> by building proactive monitoring tools, real-time alert thresholds, and rapid resolution SOPs.",
          "<strong>Creator Hardware Strategy & Adoption:</strong> Recognized hardware cost as a primary bottleneck for photographer adoption; expanded capture accessibility by introducing SDK support for lower-cost, high-image-quality hardware <strong>(Insta360 X2, X3, X4, X5 and Ricoh Theta X)</strong>, successfully lowering creator entry barriers and accelerating platform usage.",
          "<strong>Multi-Pillar Platform Scaling:</strong> Scaled Zillow's 3D Home tour volume <strong>20x (from 3,000 to 60,000+ tours/month)</strong> by driving improvements across 4 product pillars: Zillow 3D Home mobile apps, web dashboard, cloud media ingestion pipelines, and internal/external integrations.",
          "<strong>Developer Productivity & Support Automation:</strong> Conceived and launched <strong>\"Sparkle,\"</strong> a self-serve operational support tool and internal administrative API, reducing engineering support requests by <strong>87.7%</strong> and significantly increasing developer velocity.",
          "<strong>Location/Address Support Reduction:</strong> Modernized tour management APIs and address-matching workflows, cutting location/address-related support tickets by <strong>50%</strong> while improving listing sync reliability across photography and syndication partners.",
          "<strong>Field Ethnography & Creator Workflow Research:</strong> Regularly shadowed professional photographers on live real estate shoots and conducted 18 deep-dive interviews across photography companies and agents; evaluated holistic capture stacks (listing photos, drone footage, marketing videos) to eliminate multi-app friction and tailor the Zillow 3D Home app for seamless multi-media workflows.",
          "<strong>TSM & WTP Monetization Modeling:</strong> Modeled Total Serviceable Market (TSM) pricing elasticity across customer tiers and authored the executive SkyTour Distribution Strategy proposal; established a tiered product roadmap recommending the premium SkyTour product for high-WTP (Willingness to Pay) agents alongside a low-cost, lightweight tier (\"Squirrel Tours\") for price-sensitive mass-market agents.",
          "<strong>Portfolio Scaling & Multi-Product Readied Platform:</strong> Spearheaded and evangelized the strategic evolution of Zillow's immersive media suite from a single product offering into a multi-product platform; established extensible UX patterns and system architectures that accelerated time-to-market for SkyTour, Instant Floor Plans, and Unconstrained Walkthroughs.",
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Senior Product Manager, Zillow Offers Machine Learning",
        dates: "Mar 2019 - Dec 2021",
        summary:
          "<strong>Product Lead for 'Live Offers' ML Initiative</strong>. Scaled a real-time home valuation engine from concept to nationwide deployment in 24 markets, supporting a <strong>revenue leap from $1.4B to $6B</strong>. Managed intelligent routing algorithms that balanced model accuracy, delivery speed, and adverse selection risk to automate high-confidence volume while maintaining strict valuation integrity.",
        bullets: [
          "Expanded \"Live Offers\" from a single market pilot to <strong>nationwide coverage in 9 months</strong>.",
          "Achieved <strong>70% automation of \"initial offers\"</strong> (eliminating need for 25+ FTE hiring) and a <strong>20% reduction in \"adjusted offers\" variable costs</strong> through continuous refinement of risk-profile routing.",
          "Accelerated \"Time to Initial Offer\" by <strong>3.5x (from 7 days to 2 days)</strong> over 18 months through iterative experimentation and (Human-in-the-Loop) HITL process optimization.",
          "Led the \"Live Offers\" offline experiment, yielding a <strong>2x increase in home acquisitions</strong> - the most successful experiment in the program's history.",
          "Evangelized product roadmap and secured buy-in for high-impact ML initiatives through monthly business reviews (MBRs), OKR planning, and executive proposals.",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "HomeAway / Vrbo (owned by Expedia)",
    location: "Austin, TX, USA",
    dates: "Mar 2017 - Mar 2019",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Senior Product Manager, Data",
        dates: "Mar 2017 - Mar 2019",
        summary:
          "<strong>Product Lead, Data Platform & Infrastructure</strong>.  Directed HomeAway's shift to real-time, cloud-native data infrastructure and self-serve data tooling, unlocking faster decision-making and scaling data science productivity org-wide.",
        bullets: [
          "Spearheaded the development of HomeAway's cloud-native, real-time data streaming architecture, <strong>reducing 'time to insight' by over 90% (from 36 hours to under 3)</strong>. This mission-critical infrastructure powered real-time user personalization, marketing spend optimization, and high-velocity A/B testing.",
          "Orchestrated the end-to-end launch of an internal Data Catalog platform, following a rigorous <strong>'build vs. buy' analysis</strong> and iterative discovery process. By prioritizing <strong>data democratization</strong>, the application empowered 50+ Data Scientists to self-serve, reclaiming <strong>300+ productivity hours</strong> by eliminating manual data-discovery bottlenecks.",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "The Advisory Board Company (owned by Optum)",
    location: "Austin, TX, USA",
    dates: "Mar 2012 - Feb 2017",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Senior Product Manager / Product Manager",
        dates: "Mar 2012 - Feb 2017",
        summary:
          "<strong>Product Lead - Healthcare Business Intelligence</strong>. Scaled a premier Healthcare BI platform to <strong>$65M ARR</strong>, achieving <strong>6x revenue growth</strong> and a <strong>5x increase in membership</strong> (from 50 to 330+ organizations) over 4 years. Launched five strategic modules utilized by strategic planners across <strong>1,100+ US hospitals</strong>.",
        bullets: [
          "<strong>Orchestrated four critical product pivots</strong> in collaboration with R&D and UX, consistently increasing or sustaining revenue and membership.",
          "<strong>Ad-Hoc Reporting:</strong> Developed a custom data model and streamlined ETL processes, leveraging continuous user feedback to maximize module utility.",
          "<strong>Geo-Visualization:</strong> Directed the R&D of a thematic mapping tool for population and disease incidence, enabling hospital planners to identify high-growth revenue opportunities.",
          "<strong>Market Trend Analytics:</strong> Spearheaded a trend analysis tool to optimize referral patterns and patient-sharing behavior between PCPs and specialists.",
          "<strong>Predictive Forecasting:</strong> Delivered an advanced demand-forecasting and scenario-planning tool, equipping Sales with a competitive edge and empowering hospital executives with financial decision-making data.",
          "Drove <strong>product discovery</strong> by synthesizing NPS metrics and qualitative interviews; partnered with UX on iterative design sprints and usability testing to optimize the end-to-end user journey.",
          "Evangelized product roadmap through <strong>customer webinars and sales demo</strong> alignment, while providing leadership with data-driven updates on product performance and milestones.",
          "<strong>Team Leadership & Scale</strong>: Doubled a global product team (from 2 to 4) and mentored four individuals to accelerate team maturity and organizational scale.",
        ],
      },
      {
        title: "Senior Business Intelligence Analyst",
        summary:
          "Built self-service reporting and ETL infrastructure that turned manual, bottlenecked data requests into automated, real-time decision-support tools for analytics and product teams.",
        bullets: [
          "Developed and deployed a C#/ASP.NET self-service reporting tool that automated manual data requests, saving <strong>$75K</strong> in annual costs. The solution eliminated reporting bottlenecks for a 25-person team, reclaiming <strong>900+ productivity hours</strong> previously lost to manual analysis.",
          "Engineered an automated ETL pipeline using C# to ingest product usage telemetry, transforming raw logs into a comprehensive SSRS dashboard. This enabled the Product Management team to leverage real-time user behavior data, driving data-validated decisions for the feature roadmap.",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Macquarie Energy LLC",
    location: "Houston, TX, USA",
    dates: "Feb 2010 - Feb 2012",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Software Engineer, Energy Market Data Team",
        dates: "Feb 2010 - Feb 2012",
        summary:
          "Built core data-ingestion infrastructure and led a high-stakes vendor replacement, powering analytics, forecasting, and invoice settlement across energy markets.",
        bullets: [
          "Implemented Java-based <strong>ETL data feeds</strong> to fetch weather, energy market & invoice data from diverse data vendors & Independent System Operators (ISO) into internal IT systems to <strong>facilitate analytics, forecasting, invoice reconciliation & settlement</strong>.",
          "Orchestrated the successful replacement of a high-cost vendor platform with a proprietary in-house ISO Portal, <strong>delivering $500K in annual cost savings</strong>. Navigated aggressive project milestones to ensure a seamless transition, earning the <strong>ITG Award for Outstanding Delivery</strong> (May 2011) for exceptional execution.",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    name: "Wipro Technologies",
    location: "Bangalore, India / Stockholm, Sweden",
    dates: "Aug 2005 - Apr 2008",
    roles: [
      {
        title: "Senior Developer / Maintenance Lead",
        dates: "Aug 2005 - Apr 2008",
        summary:
          "Transformed production support operations and built integration infrastructure for an enterprise inventory management system, improving both customer satisfaction and system interoperability.",
        bullets: [
          "Elevated Customer Satisfaction ratings from <strong>5/7 to 6/7</strong> by transforming Production Support operations. Optimized defect resolution workflows to address high-priority issues swiftly and established a seamless pipeline for change requests, ensuring rapid delivery in subsequent releases.",
          "Engineered a robust PL/SQL integration layer for an enterprise inventory management system, enabling seamless data interoperability across disparate legacy platforms.",
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
];

const education = [
  {
    school: "Texas A&M University, Mays Business School",
    location: "College Station, TX, USA",
    degree: "Master of Science in Management of Information Systems, GPA 4.0",
    dates: "Dec 2009",
  },
  {
    school: "Anna University, Kumaraguru College of Technology",
    location: "Coimbatore, Tamilnadu, India",
    degree: "Bachelor of Engineering in Computer Science, GPA 4.0",
    dates: "Jun 2005",
  },
];
---

<Layout title="Experience">
  <h1>Experience</h1>

  <section>
    <p class="narrative">
      {/* Replace with a 2-3 sentence summary of your career arc and what you're focused on now. */}
      A short narrative summary goes here — your career arc in a few sentences,
      and what you're focused on today.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Work History</h2>
    {companies.map((company) => (
      <div class="company">
        <div class="company-header">
          <h3>{company.name}</h3>
          <span class="muted">{company.location} · {company.dates}</span>
        </div>

        {company.roles.map((role) => (
          <div class="role">
            <h4>{role.title}{role.dates && <span class="muted"> — {role.dates}</span>}</h4>
            {role.summary && <p class="summary" set:html={role.summary} />}
            <details>
              <summary>Show details</summary>
              <ul>
                {role.bullets.map((bullet) => (
                  <li set:html={bullet} />
                ))}
              </ul>
            </details>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Core Competencies</h2>
    <ul class="pill-list">
      {coreCompetencies.map((item) => (
        <li>{item}</li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    {education.map((edu) => (
      <div class="edu">
        <h3>{edu.school}</h3>
        <p class="muted">{edu.location}</p>
        <p>{edu.degree} · {edu.dates}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .pill-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .pill-list li {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .company {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .company:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .company-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.3rem 1rem;
  }

  .company-header h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .company-header .muted {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .role {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .role h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .role ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .role li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .narrative {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .summary {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  details summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    list-style: none;
  }

  details summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  details summary::before {
    content: "+ ";
  }

  details[open] summary::before {
    content: "− ";
  }

  .edu {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
</style>
